      "id": "qvrsu78",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Classification of Rivers of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Indian river systems are primarily classified into Himalayan and Peninsular rivers based on their origin.",
        "The Himalayan River System includes major perennial rivers like the Ganga and its extensive network of tributaries.",
        "Peninsular rivers are categorized based on their flow direction into East Flowing and West Flowing rivers.",
        "Drainage patterns in India reflect the geological structure, slope, and climatic conditions of the region.",
        "River valley projects and major dams serve key irrigation, hydroelectric, and flood control purposes."
      ],
      "id": "kefodgi"
    },
